yaml/key/null
description: The null key — a null scalar in key position
- >
  `~: v` is a KEYED entry whose key is null — a real entry, addressed by the null key, of which
  a mapping holds at most ONE. An EMPTY key (`: v`) spells the same null key; the quoted `'~'`
  is instead the literal-tilde STRING key:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  ~: the null key
  : the same null key, empty spelling
  '~': the string key "~"
